S += [P('Certificate', 'PreTitle'), P('This is to certify that the Major Project titled <b>“AI Legal Document Intelligence Platform”</b> is a bonafide work carried out by the students listed on the cover page, under my supervision, in partial fulfilment of the requirements for the award of the degree of Bachelor of Technology in Computer Science and Engineering at Jaypee Institute of Information Technology, Noida.', 'Body'), Spacer(1,2.5*cm), P('Signature of Supervisor: __________________________', 'Body'), P('Name: '+MENTOR, 'Body'), P('Date: __________________________', 'Body'), PageBreak(), P('Declaration of Originality', 'PreTitle'), P('We declare that this report is our original work. All published or unpublished material used from other sources has been properly acknowledged in the references. The software prototype, evaluation workflow, diagrams and implementation descriptions included in this report represent the current state of the project. Where functionality is proposed rather than completed, it is explicitly marked as future work. The project is a document-analysis prototype and is not represented as a substitute for professional legal advice.', 'Body'), Spacer(1,1.5*cm), P('Student signatures: ________________________________________________________________', 'Body'), PageBreak(), P('Acknowledgement', 'PreTitle'), P('We sincerely thank our project supervisor, '+MENTOR+', for guidance, technical feedback and encouragement throughout the project. We also acknowledge the Department of Computer Science and Engineering and Information Technology, Jaypee Institute of Information Technology, Noida, for providing the academic environment required for this work. We are grateful to the open-source and research communities whose tools and literature made this prototype possible.', 'Body'), PageBreak(), P('Abstract', 'PreTitle'), P('Legal agreements are long and hierarchical documents in which a user question may depend on definitions, exceptions, schedules, annexures and cross-referenced clauses. Conventional search identifies words but does not expose these dependencies; generic large-language-model chat systems can instead produce a convincing answer without showing whether the decisive evidence was present. This project develops an AI Legal Document Intelligence Platform for evidence-first contract question answering, risk review and controlled clause redlining.', 'Body'), P('The platform parses uploaded PDFs into page-linked clauses, stores semantic representations in ChromaDB, and constructs a lightweight Contract Graph from explicit references such as “Section 4.1” and “Schedule A”. For a question, semantic and lexical candidates are selected, related clauses are expanded through the graph, and a dependency-completeness gate verifies whether needed supporting material is available. Only then is a bounded evidence packet sent to a Groq-hosted language model for a cited, plain-language answer. The platform can abstain when a required schedule, exhibit, definition or clause is absent, rather than guess its contents. A separate Policy Graph supports document-type-specific review checks and controlled negotiation alternatives.', 'Body'), P('The key research contribution is not legal automation; it is a testable guardrail for distinguishing “relevant text was retrieved” from “sufficient evidence exists to answer”. The prototype was tested across upload/parsing, retrieval, conversational follow-up, missing-evidence, risk review, redline and error-handling scenarios. Results demonstrate an auditable end-to-end workflow over four representative agreement types. The system remains decision support only; all legal interpretations and generated changes require human review.', 'Body'), P('<b>Keywords:</b> Legal document intelligence, RAG, GraphRAG, ChromaDB, contract analysis, grounded generation, evidence verification, safe abstention.', 'Body'), PageBreak()]

